Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: a game started again from a state still vibrates (the actuator alignment defaults to the DualShock 2's)

The actuator alignment (scePadSetActAlign) is host memory and the guest sets it once, before a state is saved: a process that loads the state (the settings' Restart to apply) never has it, so every scePadSetActDirect read as no motor and the game's vibration was dead after a restart. A port with nothing aligned now reads byte 0 as the small motor and byte 1 as the large one, as the game aligns them.

--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp
@@ -723,7 +723,15 @@ namespace ps2_stubs
         ps2x::sonypad::Motors motors;
         {
             std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(g_actMutex);
-            motors = ps2x::sonypad::decodeActDirect(g_actAlign[port], data);
+            // (A game started again from a state - the settings' restart - does not call scePadSetActAlign again: the guest did before the
+            // state was saved, and the alignment is host memory. A port with nothing aligned then reads the DualShock 2's own: byte 0 the
+            // small motor, byte 1 the large one.)
+            static const uint8_t kDualShock2[6] = {0u, 1u, 0xFFu, 0xFFu, 0xFFu, 0xFFu};
+            bool none = true;
+            for (const uint8_t a : g_actAlign[port])
+                if (a != 0xFFu)
+                    none = false;
+            motors = ps2x::sonypad::decodeActDirect(none ? kDualShock2 : g_actAlign[port], data);
         }
         ps2x::sonypad::setGuestMotors(port, motors);
         setReturnS32(ctx, 1);
